  "text": "```python\ndef wsp_intersection(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the intersection of two half-open integer intervals (start, end).\n    \n    Args:\n        a: Tuple (start_a, end_a)\n        b: Tuple (start_b, end_b)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Tuple (start, end) representing the intersection, or None if empty.\n    \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any input interval is reversed (start >= end).\n    \"\"\"\n    def validate_interval(interval):\n        if not isinstance(interval, tuple) or len(interval) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a tuple of two integers.\")\n        start, end = interval\n        if start >= end:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Reversed input interval: {interval}\")\n        return start, end\n\n    start_a, end_a = validate_interval(a)\n    start_b, end_b = validate_interval(b)\n\n    # Intersection of [start_a, end_a) and [start_b, end_b)\n    # is [max(start_a, start_b), min(end_a, end_b))\n    inter_start = max(start_a, start_b)\n    inter_end = min(end_a, end_b)\n\n    if inter_start < inter_end:\n        return (inter_start, inter_end)\n    else:\n        return None\n```\n"
